From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:41:07 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 41/58] pinctrl: samsung: exynos9610: enable GPIO interrupts on
 the TOP controller

The TOP pin controller (pinctrl@139b0000, banks gpp0-gpg4) has a combined
GPIO interrupt (SPI 266) in the DT, but its samsung_pin_ctrl entry has no
.eint_gpio_init, so no interrupt domain is created and gpiod_to_irq()
returns -ENXIO for every pin in it. The display TE input gpc2-3 needs it
(M7.2 D2a: "error -6: te irq"). Add exynos_eint_gpio_init as the gs101 and
exynos2200 tables do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I8ffcc71c03aa568a67551cad6caa791c5eb475db
---
 drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
index 49210a31f..4a7a08e72 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos-arm64.c
@@ -1716,6 +1716,7 @@ static const struct samsung_pin_ctrl exynos9610_pin_ctrl[] __initconst = {
 		/* pin-controller instance 4 TOP data */
 		.pin_banks	= exynos9610_pin_banks4,
 		.nr_banks	= ARRAY_SIZE(exynos9610_pin_banks4),
+		.eint_gpio_init = exynos_eint_gpio_init,
 		.suspend	= exynos_pinctrl_suspend,
 		.resume		= exynos_pinctrl_resume,
 	}, {
